// Order and payment state machines (flowchart-diagram)
// Rules enforced centrally in OrderStateMachine. Source: order-service/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md

title Order and Payment State Machines

Created [shape: oval, label: "CREATED"]
Pending [label: "PENDING"]
Paid [label: "PAID"]
Failed [label: "FAILED"]
Cancelled [shape: oval, label: "CANCELLED"]
Expired [shape: oval, label: "EXPIRED"]
RefundPending [label: "REFUND_PENDING"]
Refunded [shape: oval, label: "REFUNDED / PARTIALLY_REFUNDED"]

Created > Pending: initiate - checkout session created
Created > Paid: free course - SYSTEM, no gateway
Created > Expired: sweeper - past expires_at
Created > Cancelled: user cancels
Pending > Paid: signed webhook captured, or sweeper reads provider
Pending > Failed: webhook failed
Pending > Expired: sweeper - past expires_at
Pending > Cancelled: user cancels
Failed > Pending: user retries - new payments row, same order
Failed > Paid: late capture - webhook or sweeper only
Expired > Paid: late capture - webhook or sweeper only
Cancelled > Paid: late capture - webhook or sweeper only
Paid > RefundPending: admin refund (one in flight per order)
RefundPending > Refunded: provider confirms - webhook, sweeper, or synchronous API response
RefundPending > Paid: provider rejects the refund
Refunded > RefundPending: partial refund - admin refunds the remainder

PayInitiated [shape: oval, label: "payment INITIATED"]
PayAuthorized [label: "AUTHORIZED - modelled, skipped by auto-capture"]
PayCaptured [label: "CAPTURED"]
PayFailed [shape: oval, label: "payment FAILED"]
PayRefunded [shape: oval, label: "REFUNDED / PARTIALLY_REFUNDED"]

PayInitiated > PayAuthorized
PayAuthorized > PayCaptured
PayInitiated > PayFailed
PayAuthorized > PayFailed
PayCaptured > PayRefunded
